 punished it. Black's winning chances go from 79% to 48%.","points":["White answers 34.Rd4: the rook takes the open d-file, aiming at the knight on d7.","Better was 33…Qa6 (−3.63), which moves the attacked queen to safety."],"better":"33…Qa6 wins a pawn, picking it up with 34…Qxd3, and gets the queen out of the way of Rxa4. After 34.Rc3 Qxd3 35.Rxd3 Nxe5 36.Rd8+ Kh7, the queens come off and Black comes out a pawn up (−3.63)."},{"ply":67,"name":"34.Qd6","cls":"mistake","color":"w","headline":"34.Qd6 is a mistake: White's winning chances go from 52% to 39%.","points":["Black answers 34…Ra4.","Better was 34.Rd4 (+0.21): the rook takes the open d-file, aiming at the knight on d7."],"better":"34.Rd4 threatens Rxd7, winning a knight, and stops …Nxe5. After 34…Nf8 35.Rd8 Qe7 36.Qd6 Qxd6 37.exd6 f5, the queens come off (+0.21)."},{"ply":72,"name":"36…Kh7","cls":"blunder","color":"b","headline":"36…Kh7 is a blunder: Black's winning chances go from 61% to 9%.","points":["White answers 37.Qxd7, which takes the knight on d7.","After Qxd7, White wins 5 points of material within 4 moves.","Better was 36…Rb2 (−1.22): the rook takes the open b-file."],"better":"36…Rb2 threatens …Qb1+, winning a rook, picking it up with 38…Rxb4, and takes the open b-file. After 37.Rxb2 Qxb2 38.f4 Qb1+ 39.Kf2 Qxe4 40.Qxd7 Qc2+, the rooks are traded (−1.22)."},{"ply":74,"name":"37…c5","cls":"mistake","color":"b","headline":"37…c5 is a mistake: Black's winning chances go from 8% to 0%. It allows mate in 4.","points":["White answers 38.Nf6+, which gives check, so the reply is forced.","The pawn on c5 can be taken by the knight on e4.","Better was 37…Rxe4 (+6.67), which takes the knight on e4."],"better":"37…Rxe4 stops the mate threat Nf6+. After 38.Rxe4 Qb1+ 39.Re1 Qf5 40.Qxc6 Qd3+, Black is a piece down (+6.67)."}],"opening":{"name":"Queen's Gambit Declined","eco":"D30","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 8.Nb3: 15 moves in all, 8 by White and 7 by Black.","Theory runs out after 8.Nb3: 